From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bigjakk <6015188+bigjakk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: kcc: cache the vsync interval in DCompPresenter when GPU vsync is off

Stock behaviour
---------------
ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.cc, DCompPresenter::EnqueuePendingFrame(), called
from DCompPresenter::Present() for every frame on the GPU main thread.
When use_gpu_vsync_ is false (features::UseGpuVsync(): --disable-gpu-vsync
or GpuVsync disabled) it does

  last_vsync_time_ = base::TimeTicks::Now();
  last_vsync_interval_ = VSyncThreadWin::GetInstance()->GetVsyncInterval();

VSyncThreadWin is VSyncThreadWinDXGI unless UseCompositorClockVSyncInterval
is enabled (off by default). VSyncThreadWinDXGI::GetVsyncInterval()
(ui/gl/vsync_thread_win_dxgi.cc) picks by OS version:

  static bool use_sv3_workaround =
      base::win::GetVersion() > base::win::Version::WIN11_22H2;

- newer than Windows 11 22H2: VSyncProviderWin::GetVSyncIntervalIfAvailable()
  -> TryGetVsyncIntervalFromDisplayConfig(nullptr) ->
  MonitorFromWindow(primary), GetMonitorInfo(), then
  display::win::GetDisplayConfigPathInfo(): GetDisplayConfigBufferSizes(),
  two std::vector allocations, QueryDisplayConfig(QDC_ONLY_ACTIVE_PATHS) and
  one DisplayConfigGetDeviceInfo() per active path until the primary is
  found. DwmGetCompositionTimingInfo / EnumDisplaySettings are only fallbacks.
- 22H2 and older: GetVSyncParametersIfAvailable() ->
  DwmGetCompositionTimingInfo(), with the QueryDisplayConfig path as fallback.

So with --disable-gpu-vsync every present pays for a display-configuration
query that goes to win32k. The owner's trace shows it at about 30 us per
frame with spikes of 0.45-1.35 ms, on the GPU main thread that is already
67-74% busy.

What consumes the value: CheckPendingFrames() puts it in
gfx::PresentationFeedback(last_vsync_time_, last_vsync_interval_, kVSync).
From there SkiaOutputSurfaceImpl::BufferPresented() forwards it to
RootCompositorFrameSinkImpl::SetDisplayVSyncParameters(), which feeds
BeginFrameSource::OnUpdateVSyncParameters() (BackToBackBeginFrameSource just
stores it as the nominal interval of its BeginFrameArgs;
DelayBasedBeginFrameSource uses it as its tick interval), and it travels in
FrameTimingDetails to clients for metrics and presentation-time bookkeeping
(viz::Display also uses it as the tolerance when sanitising timestamps).
Nothing aligns to a real vblank here: the timebase in this mode is
"now at present", not a vsync time. A value that is stale for up to one
refresh period after the primary display's refresh rate changes only means
those estimates use the old rate for that long.

Change
------
With KccCacheVsyncInterval enabled the presenter reuses
last_vsync_interval_ and calls GetVsyncInterval() again only when
refresh_ms have passed since the last query (new member
kcc_vsync_interval_query_time_), or when the cached interval is zero (the
last query failed; stock would also retry on the next present).
In this mode nothing else writes last_vsync_interval_: the presenter only
registers as a VSyncThreadWin observer when use_gpu_vsync_ is true, so
HandleVSyncOnMainThread() never runs.

All state is touched on the thread that calls Present() (GPU main), the same
one that already owns last_vsync_time_/last_vsync_interval_.

Gating / A-B
------------
base::Feature KccCacheVsyncInterval, disabled by default, file-local.
FeatureParam refresh_ms (int, default 1000, clamped to 100..10000). Feature
state and param are read once (function-local static). With the feature off
the query happens on every present exactly as before.
  --enable-features=KccCacheVsyncInterval
  --enable-features=KccCacheVsyncInterval:refresh_ms/250
Only has an effect together with --disable-gpu-vsync.
Measure: number and duration of "WinVSyncProvider::GetVSyncIntervalIfAvailable"
slices (trace category gpu) under DCompPresenter::Present - expect one per
refresh_ms instead of one per frame - plus GPU main-thread time per frame
and 1% low frame times. Sanity check: change the primary display's refresh
rate while running; presentation keeps working and the interval reported in
PresentationFeedback follows within refresh_ms.

Platforms: Windows only (dcomp_presenter.* are in the is_win sources of
ui/gl/BUILD.gn; nothing else is touched).

Not verified
------------
- Nothing was compiled.
- The per-call cost figures are from the owner's trace, not re-measured.

Build and check status (2026-11-21)
  - Compiled without any change on Windows, in the Electron 45.4.1 DCHECK
    build (dcheck_always_on) and in the official Release build (dist.zip).
  - DCHECK build: Not exercised: without a GPU DCompPresenter is not used, and
    GetVSyncIntervalIfAvailable ran 0 times with the switch off and on. The
    build only showed that it runs with the switch on.
  - Release build (dist.zip): not exercised either (0 calls with the switch
    off and on).
  - Not checked: everything the patch does; it needs a GPU with
    --disable-gpu-vsync.
The "not compiled" / "not verified" notes above were written before the
build; they stay for the caveats they list. Details and raw logs:
patches/electron-45/RESULTS.md and results/.

diff --git a/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.cc b/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.cc
index c66c1319f2939b032594d3242cbc7bef1db85474..fd8b2374ba74ae11b46a6a8dce0cf880f440b372 100644
--- a/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.cc
+++ b/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.cc
@@ -6,13 +6,16 @@
 
 #include <winerror.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <memory>
 #include <string_view>
 #include <utility>
 
 #include "base/debug/crash_logging.h"
 #include "base/debug/dump_without_crashing.h"
+#include "base/feature_list.h"
 #include "base/functional/bind.h"
+#include "base/metrics/field_trial_params.h"
 #include "base/strings/string_number_conversions.h"
 #include "base/task/single_thread_task_runner.h"
 #include "base/trace_event/trace_event.h"
@@ -113,6 +116,26 @@ constexpr bool CommitErrorReasonStringsFitInCrashKey() {
 static_assert(CommitErrorReasonStringsFitInCrashKey(),
               "Commit error reason strings must fit in a Size64 crash key.");
 
+// KCC: when GPU vsync is off (--disable-gpu-vsync) EnqueuePendingFrame() asks
+// VSyncThreadWin for the vsync interval on every present, which on current
+// Windows 11 is a QueryDisplayConfig() round trip. With this feature the
+// presenter reuses the last answer and asks again at most once per
+// |refresh_ms| (default 1000, clamped to 100..10000).
+BASE_FEATURE(kKccCacheVsyncInterval, base::FEATURE_DISABLED_BY_DEFAULT);
+constexpr base::FeatureParam<int> kKccCacheVsyncIntervalRefreshMs{
+    &kKccCacheVsyncInterval, "refresh_ms", 1000};
+
+// How long a queried vsync interval may be reused. Zero when the feature is
+// disabled, i.e. query on every present as upstream does.
+base::TimeDelta KccVsyncIntervalRefreshPeriod() {
+  static const base::TimeDelta period =
+      base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(kKccCacheVsyncInterval)
+          ? base::Milliseconds(
+                std::clamp(kKccCacheVsyncIntervalRefreshMs.Get(), 100, 10000))
+          : base::TimeDelta();
+  return period;
+}
+
 }  // namespace
 
 DCompPresenter::PendingFrame::PendingFrame(PresentationCallback callback)
@@ -345,7 +368,16 @@ void DCompPresenter::EnqueuePendingFrame(PresentationCallback callback) {
     StartOrStopVSyncThread();
   } else {
     last_vsync_time_ = base::TimeTicks::Now();
-    last_vsync_interval_ = VSyncThreadWin::GetInstance()->GetVsyncInterval();
+    // KCC: see kKccCacheVsyncInterval. In this mode nothing else writes
+    // |last_vsync_interval_| (the presenter never observes the vsync thread),
+    // so it doubles as the cached value. A zero interval means the last query
+    // failed; retry on the next present as upstream would.
+    const base::TimeDelta refresh_period = KccVsyncIntervalRefreshPeriod();
+    if (refresh_period.is_zero() || last_vsync_interval_.is_zero() ||
+        last_vsync_time_ - kcc_vsync_interval_query_time_ >= refresh_period) {
+      last_vsync_interval_ = VSyncThreadWin::GetInstance()->GetVsyncInterval();
+      kcc_vsync_interval_query_time_ = last_vsync_time_;
+    }
     // Handle pending frames asynchronously to avoid reentrancy issues in the
     // caller.
     task_runner_->PostTask(FROM_HERE,
diff --git a/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.h b/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.h
index 6d7a4636c53a37799c2211577f8b3591e929763d..c7f9a7b3d11c84c619ab18ac0e02b5e497741b6c 100644
--- a/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.h
+++ b/ui/gl/dcomp_presenter.h
@@ -140,6 +140,10 @@ class GL_EXPORT DCompPresenter : public Presenter,
   base::TimeTicks last_vsync_time_;
   base::TimeDelta last_vsync_interval_;
 
+  // KCC (KccCacheVsyncInterval): when |last_vsync_interval_| was last queried
+  // from VSyncThreadWin on the non-GPU-vsync path of EnqueuePendingFrame().
+  base::TimeTicks kcc_vsync_interval_query_time_;
+
   std::unique_ptr<DCLayerTree> layer_tree_;
 
   // Set in the ctor. Indicates whether vsync is enabled for the process.
